**What changed:** Angular moved the DOM-property name remapping (previously done at runtime in `@angular/core` inside `setPropertyAndInputs` in `packages/core/src/render3/instructions/shared.ts`) from the client into the compiler. At 20.1 the runtime keeps a `mapPropName` helper whose comment now states: "Note: this mapping has to be kept in sync with the equivalent mappings in the compiler." — mapping `class`→`className`, `for`→`htmlFor`, `formaction`→`formAction`, `innerHtml`→`innerHTML`, `readonly`→`readOnly`, `tabindex`→`tabIndex` (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/56769de4d83a08b8044cd2463341cbd60d40191f/packages/core/src/render3/instructions/shared.ts). Because DOM property bindings can never resolve to a directive `@Input`, the compiler now emits the already-remapped name, "saving us some processing on the client" (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/56769de4d83a08b8044cd2463341cbd60d40191f, https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/62421). The generic `ɵɵproperty` instruction still calls `setPropertyAndInputs` for bindings that may hit inputs (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/56769de4d83a08b8044cd2463341cbd60d40191f/packages/core/src/render3/instructions/property.ts). Related JIT-only regression from this change was reported in .

**Affects:** No application code condition — internal compiler/runtime optimization; only relevant if code or tests rely on runtime name remapping, or if a third-party/JIT-compiled template bypasses the AOT remapping.

**Action:** none — re-verify that property bindings such as `[class]`, `[for]`, `[innerHtml]`, `[readonly]`, `[tabindex]`, `[formaction]` still apply correctly at runtime, especially in JIT or 3rd-party precompiled templates.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// shared.ts (Angular 20.1) — remapping retained only as a runtime fallback,
// now duplicated in the compiler.
function mapPropName(name: string): string {
  if (name === 'class') return 'className';
  if (name === 'for') return 'htmlFor';
  if (name === 'formaction') return 'formAction';
  if (name === 'innerHtml') return 'innerHTML';
  if (name === 'readonly') return 'readOnly';
  if (name === 'tabindex') return 'tabIndex';
  return name;
}
```

**What changed:** Previously, typed `FormGroup`/`FormRecord.reset()` accepted only standalone values or `{value, disabled}` objects per control. The new internal type `ɵFormGroupArgumentValue` (and corresponding `ɵFormRecordArgumentValue`) accepts `ɵValue<T[K]> | FormControlState<ɵValue<T[K]>` for typed forms, allowing `ControlState` (i.e. `FormControlState`) as reset arguments for `FormGroup`/`FormRecord`. The `AbstractControl` class gains a 3rd generic parameter `TValueWithOptionalControlStates` to decouple the `reset` type argument from `TValue`. (<https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/55860>, <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/20.1.0/packages/forms/src/model/abstract_model.ts>, <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/20.1.0/packages/forms/src/model/form_group.ts>)

**Affects:** Applications using typed `FormGroup` or `FormRecord` and calling `reset()` with `{value: T, disabled: boolean}` objects per control, which previously failed type-checking.

**Action:** required: re-verify `reset()` calls on typed `FormGroup`/`FormRecord` to ensure type-checking passes and no `as any` or workaround casts remain needed.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
