// After (20.1.0): accepted by ɵFormGroupArgumentValue
// ɵFormGroupArgumentValue uses: ɵValue<T[K]> | FormControlState<ɵValue<T[K]>
form.reset({ first: { value: 'name', disabled: true } });
```

**What changed:** In `@angular/forms`, `SelectControlValueAccessor` (used by `select` with `ngModel`/`formControlName`/`formControl`) no longer writes the select value synchronously while individual `<option>` elements are created, removed, or re-valued. The `NgSelectOption` setters `@Input('ngValue')` and `@Input('value')` and `ngOnDestroy()` now call a new internal method `_writeValueAfterRender()` instead of `this._select.writeValue(this._select.value)`. `_writeValueAfterRender()` queues a single deferred write via `afterNextRender({write: () => this.writeValue(this.value)}, {injector: this.appRefInjector})`, guarded by a `_queuedWrite` flag and `DestroyRef.destroyed` checks; `writeValue` itself now also calls `this.cdr.markForCheck()` (new `ChangeDetectorRef`, `ApplicationRef`, `DestroyRef` injections) (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/4f0221e1933675b24bdbf95be3825fdacee13c00). This cuts the previously exponential number of `_compareWith`/`_compareValue` calls when adding/removing options (e.g. 501,001 calls for 1000 options with the 500th selected, now roughly one per option until a match) (https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/41330), and fixes delayed option removal with `@angular/animations`, where the browser snapped the select to the first option after the matching option was removed from the DOM (issue #18430) (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/61949).

