**Action:** required: re-verify select value rendering in tests and runtime — after `fixture.detectChanges()`, flush the deferred write (e.g. `tick()` under `fakeAsync`, or `await fixture.whenStable()`/`fixture.whenRenderStable()`) before asserting `select.nativeElement.value` or `option.nativeElement.selected`; if a spec constructs `SelectControlValueAccessor` directly, wrap it in `TestBed.runInInjectionContext` with a `ChangeDetectorRef` provider (as the Angular test suite itself was updated to do). Also re-verify that when a bound option list no longer contains the selected model value you update the model yourself — per the commit, "The model value still needs to be updated to a valid value when the selected value is deleted or it will be out of sync with the DOM" (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/4f0221e1933675b24bdbf95be3825fdacee13c00). No dependency, build, or template changes are required.

**Before/after:**
